# An `X "c"` hint names the literal terminal whose one byte is c, however
# the literal spells it ("\x3a" is ":"); here the hint decides nothing.
# error: dead_x_hint_escaped_literal.grammar:20:
# error: X ":" on name
# error: has no effect
@lexer
tokens
    ident
    colon
    eof
    err
':'                                         → colon
[a-zA-Z]+                                   → ident
.                                           → err
@parser
# (no @conflicts block: the grammar must be conflict-free)
program! = entry "\x3a" IDENT               → (entry 1 3)
         | entry                            → (entry 1)
entry    = name                             → 1
name     = IDENT X ":"                      → 1
